# ===================================================================
# .dockerignore — what NEVER goes into the image.
#
# This is not the same job as .gitignore. Git decides what gets
# SHARED; this decides what gets BUILT INTO a thing that runs on a
# stranger's machine. Every extra file here makes the image bigger and
# slower to pull, and tells anyone who pulls it more than they need to
# know.
# ===================================================================

# Version control history. Megabytes, and none of it runs.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Host-specific link files.
.netlify/

# Editors and OS junk.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.log

# This Dockerfile's own build context has no README/docs worth shipping
# into a container whose only job is to serve HTML.
*.md
